### 1. Create donor
POST http://localhost:8080/api/donors
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Campus Canteen", "contact": "9999999999" }

### 1a. Update donor
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/donors/1
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Campus Canteen Main", "contact": "9999990000" }

### 2. Create NGO 1
POST http://localhost:8080/api/ngos
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Hope Shelter", "contact": "8888888888" }

### 2a. Update NGO
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/ngos/1
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Hope Shelter Central", "contact": "8888880000" }

### 3. Create NGO 2 (for the "only one NGO" test)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/ngos
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Care Foundation", "contact": "7777777777" }

### 4. Donor lists food -> 201
POST http://localhost:8080/api/listings
Content-Type: application/json

{ "donorId": 1, "foodType": "Rice", "quantity": 10.5, "safeUntil": "2026-12-31T23:00:00" }

### 5. Browse listings (pagination + sorting) -> 200
GET http://localhost:8080/api/listings?page=0&size=5&sortBy=quantity

### 6. NGO 1 claims listing 1 -> 201
POST http://localhost:8080/api/listings/1/claim
Content-Type: application/json

{ "ngoId": 1 }

### 7. EDGE: NGO 2 claims same listing -> 409 (already claimed)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/listings/1/claim
Content-Type: application/json

{ "ngoId": 2 }

### 8. Mark listing collected -> 200
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/listings/1/collect

### 9. EDGE: collect again -> 409
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/listings/1/collect

### 10. Monthly report -> 200 (change month if needed)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/reports/monthly?year=2026&month=9

### 11. EDGE: invalid input (blank type, negative qty, past date) -> 400
POST http://localhost:8080/api/listings
Content-Type: application/json

{ "donorId": 1, "foodType": "", "quantity": -5, "safeUntil": "2020-01-01T10:00:00" }

### 12. EDGE: unknown listing -> 404
POST http://localhost:8080/api/listings/999/claim
Content-Type: application/json

{ "ngoId": 1 }

### 13. EDGE: bad sort field -> 400
GET http://localhost:8080/api/listings?sortBy=abc

### 14. Auto-expire test: creates a listing that expires in 1 minute (safeUntil is auto-set)
< {%
    const d = new Date(Date.now() + 60 * 1000 - new Date().getTimezoneOffset() * 60000);
    request.variables.set("soon", d.toISOString().slice(0, 19));
%}
POST http://localhost:8080/api/listings
Content-Type: application/json

{ "donorId": 1, "foodType": "Bread", "quantity": 3, "safeUntil": "{{soon}}" }

### 15. Run this AFTER 1-2 minutes: status is EXPIRED and claiming gives 409
GET http://localhost:8080/api/listings?sortBy=id

### 16. EDGE: claim the expired listing (use its id, e.g. 2) -> 409
POST http://localhost:8080/api/listings/2/claim
Content-Type: application/json

{ "ngoId": 1 }

### CRUD: update listing
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/listings/1
Content-Type: application/json

{ "donorId": 1, "foodType": "Updated Rice", "quantity": 12.5, "safeUntil": "2030-12-31T23:00:00" }

### CRUD: delete listing and its related claims
DELETE http://localhost:8080/api/listings/1
